WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.800
Has Ant-Man 3 been lost to the Quantum Realm
forever?

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:08.400
A source allegedly close to Marvel Studios
is reporting that a three-quel for the tiny

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:13.310
Avenger isn't going to happen, and that Ant-Man
and The Wasp may see their further adventures

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:16.140
relegated to the upcoming Disney+ streaming
service.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.699
The rumor comes courtesy of rumor monger Mikey
Sutton, who points to two reasons in particular

00:00:21.699 --> 00:00:25.990
for the decision to shrink Scott Lang and
Hope Van Dyne down from the big screen to

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:26.700
the small one.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:31.500
First, Marvel Studios head honcho Kevin Feige
is said to be preoccupied with the task of

00:00:31.509 --> 00:00:36.220
folding the X-Men and Fantastic Four, along
with the other formerly Fox-owned properties

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:40.940
recently acquired by Marvel's parent company
Disney, into the Marvel Cinematic Universe

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:44.840
— something he alluded to at San Diego Comic-Con
2019.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:50.600
Second, Sutton claims that Feige is invested
in exploring different genres with the MCU's

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:55.650
Phase 4 and Phase 5 offerings — from spy
thrillers to psychological horror flicks and

00:00:55.650 --> 00:01:00.150
everything in-between — so apparently, there
simply won't be any room left on the slate

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:02.400
for more conventional superhero adventures.

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:07.220
We submit, however, that this is nothing new
for the MCU, which has played in different

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:08.490
genres for years now …

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:11.040
"That's, uhh… naked.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:11.820
Very naked."

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:13.620
"Huh.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:18.560
That's… that's in my brain, now."

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:20.340
… but we digress.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:23.680
Let's look at this rumor from a pure common
sense standpoint.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:29.220
The "Feige is just too busy" angle has been
dragged out in one other recent situation:

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:34.920
as a pretty thin excuse on the part of Sony
Pictures CEO Tony Vinciquerra as to why his

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:38.600
studio and Disney couldn't re-up their agreement
to share custody of Spider-Man.

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:43.580
You'll notice that it's not actually Feige
complaining about how busy he is in either

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:48.460
circumstance; it's other parties putting those
words in his mouth for him, which seems a

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:49.300
little bit suspect.

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:54.280
As we alluded to before, it also doesn't make
a heck of a lot of sense to advance the notion

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:58.260
that because Marvel wants to do some different
things with some of its upcoming features

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:03.600
like the forthcoming Blade reboot legacy heroes
and/or their feature franchises must be left

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:04.100
behind.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:09.300
If that were the case, we certainly wouldn't
be getting Thor: Love and Thunder, an unprecedented

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.620
fourth film for an original Avenger.

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:16.240
One could even make the argument that Ant-Man
and his supporting characters were more important

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:20.720
to the MCU's overarching narrative through
Phase 3 than virtually any others.

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:25.020
The Ant-Man films introduced the technology
that made it possible for the Avengers to

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:29.250
travel through time and acquire all of the
Infinity Stones before Thanos could; for that

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:32.920
matter, if Lang hadn't been freed from the
Quantum Realm by the timely inter vention

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:36.760
of a mouse - the universe would be toast yes,
that’s a mouse officially.

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:42.080
The Ant-Man flicks may be the lightest and
breeziest of the MCU's franchises, but they've

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:46.560
been charged with doing a surprising amount
of narrative heavy lifting and while they

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:50.970
haven't exactly blown up the box office, they
haven't flopped, either, together totaling

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:53.940
over $1.1 billion dollars worldwide.

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:58.440
All of these points aside, it's worth considering
that a couple of sources that we know to be

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:03.810
close to Marvel Studios namely, Paul Rudd
and co-star Michael Douglas have made public

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:06.959
remarks indicating that Ant-Man 3 isn't off
the table.

00:03:06.959 --> 00:03:11.680
During a Television Critics' Association presser
back in February, Douglas indicated that while

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:16.680
nothing has been formalized, there had absolutely
been talks about Ant-Man 3, although he didn't

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:21.090
expect to hear whether it was actually going
down until, quote, "its third rewrite."

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:26.860
As for Rudd, he's simply gone on record stating
that he doesn't know when or if Ant-Man 3

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:31.160
will happen as recently as June, although
it's possible that he knows more than he's

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:31.800
letting on.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.060
So, will there be an Ant-Man 3?

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:38.660
The simple fact is that we don't know, but
we have no compelling reason right now to

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:39.820
think there won't be.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:45.330
The Ant-Man flicks have served a valuable
purpose as fun, light palate cleansers in

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:49.599
between huge, universe-shaking events, and
we think it's pretty likely that the MCU will

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:51.560
be in need of another one of those at some
point.

00:03:51.989 --> 00:03:56.819
Also, Mr. Feige, if you're watching this:
please know that if fans never get the chance

00:03:56.819 --> 00:04:01.800
to hear Lang's motor-mouthed buddy Luis recount
the events of Avengers: Endgame in his own

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:06.500
inimitable fashion, you can expect about four
million sternly worded emails.

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:08.280
"OK, sorry sorry…

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:09.290
I just — y'know, uhh…

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:09.780
I just get excited and stuff."

